#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:557
msgid "Why are my theme header and footer hidden on the checkout page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:558
msgid "This is the default distraction-free mode to increase conversion rates. You can re-enable your theme header and footer in the \"Design & Settings\" tab by checking \"Use Theme Header/Footer\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:561
msgid "If I disable the header, will I lose my tracking pixels and analytics?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:562
msgid "No! The \"distraction-free\" mode only hides the visual elements of the header and footer using CSS. The underlying WordPress <head> is still fully loaded. All your Facebook Pixels, Google Analytics, Tag Manager, and SEO meta tags will continue to work perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:565
msgid "How do I reorder checkout fields?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mcrpd-checkout-settings.php:566
msgid "Go to the \"Checkout Fields\" tab and drag the fields using the handle icon on the left side of each row."
msgstr ""

